docs(ai): correct the Fable 5 registry note — top tier, not a fast tier

The comment I shipped in the previous commit described claude-fable-5 as "the
new fast frontier model and the candidate to replace this [Haiku] lane." That is
wrong in the most expensive possible direction, and left uncorrected it would
have pointed the cheap utility lane at a $10/$50 model.

Fable 5 is Anthropic's MOST CAPABLE and most EXPENSIVE model — $10/$50 per MTok,
2x Opus 5 and 10x Haiku 4.5. It is disqualified from any cost-sensitive lane on
four independent grounds:
- thinking is always on and cannot be disabled (thinking.disabled returns 400),
  so trivial extraction still pays reasoning tokens;
- single turns can run for minutes, which is wrong for interactive surfaces;
- it requires 30-day data retention and is unavailable under ZDR;
- safety classifiers can return stop_reason 'refusal' with HTTP 200 and empty
  content, which every caller would need to branch on.

Kept the registry entry (the drift checker tracks it, and a future
hardest-reasoning surface has a named target) but rewrote the note to say what
it actually is. Nothing points at it.

No behavior change — comment only. 135 tests green, drift check passes.

